		{
			"id": "e40RHOheuSNsAhDCE",
			"description": "Power Fist",
			"local_notes": "Cannot be used to Feint, and the -2 parry reflects how slow and clumsy the servo-driven gauntlet is to reposition defensively; a GM may rule it takes a Ready maneuver to recover after a solid punch against a very hard surface (a wall, a vehicle hull). It is not a precision weapon: no combination of skill or luck lets it target a called shot at a meaningful bonus (GM's call).\n\nLore: One of the signature Astartes and Terminator melee weapons: a reinforced gauntlet with an internal power field and myo-fibre actuators, consistently shown punching clean through Astartes power armour, vehicle hulls and monstrous xenos alike - the framework's Tactical Dreadnought (DR 200) armour table entry explicitly lists the power fist as one of the few things that still kills a Terminator.\n\nDesign: Fixed anchor (Rescale, framework.md): thr+8d(10) cr. It is built from first principles rather than borrowed from a catalogue \"power glove\": because the internal actuators (not the wielder's own swing) generate most of the force, its bonus is a large flat die addition to the wielder's own thrust (thr+8d) rather than a multiplier on that thrust (a \"thr x3\"-style multiplier was considered and rejected, since it would make the weapon nearly unusable in a human's hands and absurdly swingy in an Astartes', whereas a flat die bonus keeps it dangerous regardless of wielder and matches the fiction that the fist itself, not the arm behind it, is doing the killing). Armor Divisor (10) is the shared disruption-field divisor (framework.md, power-field rule). At Astartes ST 30, thr+8d (thr 3d, so 11d, average 38.5) against Terminator plate (DR 200, eff. DR 20) penetrates every time (99.8% even against Cataphractii, DR 220) and against Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 10) always, matching \"power fist ... kills Terminators in Astartes hands\" cleanly. With the field off the gauntlet is a servo-driven fist at thr+2 cr, the mundane baseline, with the same reach C and parry -2. Handling: reach C, parry -2 and the no-Feint/no-called-shot notes encode the framework's \"power fist ... unwieldy (hard to parry, slow)\" instruction without needing a bespoke game mechanic beyond existing GURPS defense penalties; being an unarmed-style Brawling punch rather than a bladed weapon, the axe/mace \"U\" convention doesn't apply. Weight (40 lb) and min ST (15) are unchanged - already an Astartes-only figure.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "8000",
			"base_weight": "40 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "w4LJMpnyE4d1idtuA",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cr",
						"st": "thr",
						"base": "8d",
						"armor_divisor": 10
					},
					"reach": "C",
					"parry": "-2",
					"strength": "15",
					"usage": "Punch, field on",
