							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Throwing"
							}
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true
		},
		{
			"id": "eZrXpiVFfuB3EfSoq",
			"description": "Krak Grenade",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Imperium's standard anti-armour and anti-fortification grenade, issued alongside frag grenades to Guard and Astartes forces alike; codex and Black Library background repeatedly show it wrecking light vehicles and bunker firing points, and occasionally cracking heavier targets at real cost and risk.\n\nDesign: Modelled as a hand-thrown shaped charge using the same \"cr ex plus armour divisor\" logic GURPS uses for anti-tank warheads, kept well below the meltagun anchor (8dx6(10) burn to ½D) in both multiplier and divisor: a grenade-sized shaped charge carries an order of magnitude less fuel and a much less focused liner than a dedicated melta weapon's thermal lance, so it keeps the mundane armour divisor of (2) rather than melta's (10). Required vehicle-armour check against framework.md's AV-to-DR table, by exact dice distribution (6dx4, average 84, divisor 2): AV10 (DR 100, effective 50) penetrates 98.0% of hits, AV11 (DR 150, effective 75) 72.1% — both comfortably \"reliable.\" AV12 (DR 200, effective 100) drops to 14.5% — \"sometimes,\" as required. AV13 (DR 275, effective 137.5) rounds to a negligible 0.015% (only the maximum possible roll of 6d, 36, times 4 = 144, just clears it), and AV14 (DR 350, effective 175) is a flat 0% — the maximum possible roll (144) can never reach 175 at all — so a krak grenade cannot crack a Leman Russ or Land Raider's frontal armour. This matches the lore's use of krak grenades as light-vehicle and infantry-support ordnance rather than a dedicated tank-killer — that job belongs to the meltagun and melta bomb.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
